{"content":[{"c":["KABZEEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City located in the extreme south of Judah’s territory adjacent to neighboring Edom (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.15.21","r":"Josh.15.21","rawR":"Josh.15.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.15.21","value":"Josh.15.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 15:21"},"; also called Jekabzeel in ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.25","r":"Neh.11.25","rawR":"Neh.11.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.25","value":"Neh.11.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:25"},"). Benaiah, one of David’s valiant warriors, came from there (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.20","r":"2Sam.23.20","rawR":"2Sam.23.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.20","value":"2Sam.23.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:20"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.22","r":"1Chr.11.22","rawR":"1Chr.11.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.22","value":"1Chr.11.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:22"},"). The reference in Nehemiah indicates that Judah’s tribe returned to this area after the exile. Its exact site is not known, but Khirbet Hora has been suggested."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Kabzeel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jos 15:21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.15.21","rawQueryValue":"Josh.15.21","sourceRefExact":"Josh.15.21"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.25","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.25","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.25"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 23:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.23.20","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.23.20","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.23.20"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 11:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.11.22","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.11.22","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.11.22"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"1d8571d6171045724382c8c5